     "Point 4 (Waqf in al-Aʿmash & al-Dāraquṭnī's pattern): In ʿIlal 1512, the trustworthy Jarīr b. ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd narrates the report mawqūf as Abū Hurayra's word (while the main printed text prefers rafʿ, the Egyptian MS siglum 'm' reads 'the attribution to the Companion is correct'; though whether Jarīr's text contained the bone clause is unpreserved). Immediately adjacent, for the same Abū Ṣāliḥ ← Abū Hurayra chain, al-Dāraquṭnī rules in 1508 'mawqūf, wa-huwa ashbah' and in 1511 'al-mawqūf huwa al-maḥfūẓ'—proving this chain was repeatedly elevated to marfūʿ by mistake.",
